29,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It seems some of our dear neighbors in the outer wards are struggling to reach us now that the buses have changed. It would be so sad if they felt forgotten.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My findings show that remote catalogue use peaks late at night, and our previous outreach stops in the outer wards were surprisingly popular, often drawing more visitors than the main building.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that some old programs from six years ago are still going on all by themselves! Also, the old outreach stops were super popular, even more than the main library!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My research reveals a curious pattern: our one-off equipment funds are returned unused, yet our vehicle running costs are spiraling. More concerningly, the county grants only cover the first year of session fees.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"I have found that while we have skilled volunteers, we lack staff on the payroll trained to supervise outside facilitators. Furthermore, the technician responsible for power tool certification retired this spring.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, it is worrying that the grants only cover the first year. We must be careful not to start something we cannot sustain for our friends in the community.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, I agree. It is also worth noting that the high demand for remote access late at night suggests our physical walls are a barrier for many.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, that's exactly it! If people are using the catalogue at night, maybe they can't get to the library during the day. We should do something that goes to them instead!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, your enthusiasm for mobility is charming, but we must be cautious. If our vehicle costs are already overrunning, a fleet-heavy expansion might be a fiscal fantasy.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, I agree. Beyond the costs, we must consider the human element. If we expand our outreach or technical services, we need to ensure we have the qualified staff to supervise them safely.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, you are so right to think of the staff. We wouldn't want our kind volunteers to feel overwhelmed or unsupported in their efforts to help others.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, if vehicle costs are the issue, perhaps we should look for a solution that balances accessibility with efficiency, rather than simply adding more trips.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, but what if we use the things that already work? I saw that some old groups are still meeting without any help! Maybe we don't need a big expensive fleet if the community helps us.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, while community spirit is a lovely sentiment, it rarely balances a ledger. We must avoid the trap of ""invisible"" costs that suddenly appear in year two once the initial grant vanishes.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, relying on community spirit is a risk if we lack the internal capacity to manage it. Without a certified technician or trained supervisors, we cannot safely oversee technical or external programs.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I am also thinking about the weather. I found that roads north of the river closed several times last winter, which makes me worry about any plan that relies on a strict travel schedule.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
50,2,4,pass,Shizue,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that is a poignant point. Between the road closures and the bus changes, the physical distance to our branches is becoming a significant hurdle for those who need us most.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Shizue, that's why we should look at the old stuff! Some groups are still meeting even without us, so they must have a way to handle the snow and the buses!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
53,2,4,pass,Rin,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shizue, your observation regarding the roads adds a layer of logistical fragility to the financial one. It seems we are facing a trifecta of risks: unreliable transport, spiraling vehicle costs, and a funding cliff.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
55,2,4,pass,Benjamin,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
56,2,4,talk,Minako,,"We must be realistic. Between the funding cliff Benjamin mentioned and the lack of certified supervisors I discovered, any proposal requiring specialized oversight or high operational costs is a liability. We need a sustainable, low-risk model.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
57,2,4,pass,Minako,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
58,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
62,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I feel that Candidate C, the Language Learning Circles, is a lovely way to bring people together. It seems more flexible than a bus and doesn't require the expensive tools Minako mentioned.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Candidate D, the Digital Archive Portal, seems the most serene and sustainable choice. It addresses the late-night demand for remote access and bypasses the road and bus barriers Shizue and I discussed.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I like Candidate C too! It's like those old groups I found that are still meeting on their own. If we just help them, it won't cost as much as a big bus!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,I must disagree with the allure of Candidate A; it is a fiscal disaster waiting to happen given our vehicle costs and the funding cliff. Candidate B is equally problematic without a certified technician.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Minako,,I agree with Benjamin. Candidate B is impossible without a certified technician to ensure safety. Candidate A is too risky given the vehicle costs and road closures. I lean toward Candidate D for its stability.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, your point about the portal is very sensible. It would allow our neighbors to feel connected to their history even when the snow is deep or the buses do not run.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, exactly. It provides a sanctuary of knowledge that is always open, ensuring that no one is excluded simply because of where they live or the time of day.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, but a portal is just a screen! Candidate C is more like an adventure. It's like the groups I found—people helping people. That's way more exciting than just scanning old papers!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, while adventure is a delightful quality for a novel, it is a terrifying quality for a public budget. Candidate C relies on facilitators whose fees may vanish after year one, leaving us with a void.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, excitement does not replace infrastructure. Candidate C requires trained facilitators and supervision, which I have already noted we lack on our payroll. We cannot simply hope the community manages it.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Rin, your heart is in the right place, dear, but I worry about the facilitators. If they leave or the funding stops, we might disappoint the people who have come to rely on those circles.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, your concern about the funding cliff is a strong argument against Candidate C. A digital portal, however, is a lasting resource that doesn't depend on recurring session fees or physical travel.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, but I saw that the old digitisation project from six years ago was a mess! Half the pictures weren't even indexed. If we do Candidate D, we have to do it right this time!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, a messy archive is a tragedy of the past, but a bankrupt budget is a tragedy of the future. Candidate D utilizes capital items, which draw from the endowment rather than the volatile operating budget.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, the previous failure of the digitisation project is a reason to implement a structured plan, not to abandon the idea. Candidate D is the only option that doesn't create an unsustainable burden on our current staff.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I believe Candidate D is the most thoughtful choice. It protects our neighbors from the unpredictability of the roads and ensures we can keep our promises to them without worrying about the budget. I vote for D.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. Candidate D is the most inclusive and stable path forward, removing the physical and temporal barriers that currently limit our reach. I vote for D.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I still think C is more fun, but if the adults are so worried about the money and the rules, I guess D is the safest. I'll vote for D, but we have to fix the indexing! I vote for D.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,Logic dictates that we avoid the funding cliff of Candidate C and the operational hazards of A and B. Candidate D is the only rational choice that aligns with our financial structure. I vote for D.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Minako,,Candidate D is the only proposal that avoids our critical staffing gaps and financial risks. It provides a sustainable service without overloading our personnel or risking our budget. I vote for D.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
